# Unit L3 (span_arms.md rev 3.3 §14.4 L3, BACK; lanes l3feat/l3feat2, 2026-11-20): A
# REQUIRED RUN MAY BEGIN INSIDE A LOOKBEHIND, before the attempt start. TOP's BACK row
# joins the root's left guard to its head (`(?<=foo)bar` is `foobar` at K -3); the
# kit's pre-check scans from max(0, startpos + K), the entry and the VM attempt loop
# move to the hit less K (signed), an end clamp answers NOMATCH where the hit less K
# passes the subject's end, and the forward scan's re-entry (`handoff`) is DECLINED at
# K < 0 (W-L17, R-1). Every block on the default route and under `engine vm`, cells
# at every start position. Expectations from libpcre2-8 10.46 through
# tests/litscan/gen_handoff.py's ctypes oracle (`pcre_cells`), byte blocks
# cross-checked against python3 `re` (the two must agree; `# pcre2-only` where
# python cannot compile the pattern or the block is utf8), never pcrec's.
# W-L1 (span_arms §5.7 and §14.4 L3, the kit's witness): the run `foobar` begins 3 bytes before every match (K -3); the kit scans from max(0, startpos - 3), so a search from 2 or 3 finds the run at 0 and the match at 3; a scan from the start offset misses it
pattern (?<=foo)bar
features all
encoding byte
ms 0 "foobar" 3 6
ms 1 "foobar" 3 6
ms 2 "foobar" 3 6
ms 3 "foobar" 3 6
ns 4 "foobar"
ns 5 "foobar"
ns 6 "foobar"
ms 0 "xfoobarfoobar" 4 7
ms 1 "xfoobarfoobar" 4 7
ms 2 "xfoobarfoobar" 4 7
ms 3 "xfoobarfoobar" 4 7
ms 4 "xfoobarfoobar" 4 7
ms 5 "xfoobarfoobar" 10 13
ms 6 "xfoobarfoobar" 10 13
ms 7 "xfoobarfoobar" 10 13
ms 8 "xfoobarfoobar" 10 13
ms 9 "xfoobarfoobar" 10 13
ms 10 "xfoobarfoobar" 10 13
ns 11 "xfoobarfoobar"
ns 12 "xfoobarfoobar"
ns 13 "xfoobarfoobar"
ms 0 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 1 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 2 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 3 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 4 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 5 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 6 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 7 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ms 8 "foobafoobar" 8 11
ns 9 "foobafoobar"
ns 10 "foobafoobar"
ns 11 "foobafoobar"
ns 0 "fobar"
ns 1 "fobar"
ns 2 "fobar"
ns 3 "fobar"
ns 4 "fobar"
ns 5 "fobar"
ns 0 "barfoo"
ns 1 "barfoo"
ns 2 "barfoo"
ns 3 "barfoo"
ns 4 "barfoo"
ns 5 "barfoo"
ns 6 "barfoo"

